WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.355
For a developer extracting refunds, a plausible answer can quietly become bad data.

00:00:06.355 --> 00:00:12.610
RouteWise helps choose the lowest-cost NVIDIA Nemotron configuration that the workload evidence supports,

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:14.535
using Nebius Token Factory.

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:18.023
This is a real recorded synthetic conversation.

00:00:18.023 --> 00:00:21.077
The previous route released a missing issue date.

00:00:21.077 --> 00:00:25.276
The adopted profile resolves the store’s statement from its own timestamp.

00:00:25.276 --> 00:00:29.858
It keeps the refund issue date separate from when the money arrives.

00:00:29.858 --> 00:00:32.530
The source and both outputs remain inspectable.

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:38.999
When the conversation does not determine one calendar date, RouteWise holds the answer

00:00:38.999 --> 00:00:40.302
for human review.

00:00:40.302 --> 00:00:45.082
Every model call, raw answer, normalization, and validation check is visible.

00:00:45.082 --> 00:00:48.993
Passing a validator is not a guarantee of correctness.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:54.396
Declare quality and latency requirements, then inspect matched alternatives.

00:00:54.396 --> 00:01:01.324
The adopted profile combines grounded Nano, selective Super escalation, and deterministic date normalization.

00:01:01.324 --> 00:01:08.252
On three hundred twelve representative synthetic conversations, it completed ninety-eight point four percent

00:01:08.252 --> 00:01:12.515
correctly without review, with zero observed wrong releases.

00:01:12.515 --> 00:01:16.246
Review and task accuracy are reported separately.

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:22.938
Tighten the deadline to twenty-five hundred milliseconds, and fixed Super becomes the measured

00:01:22.938 --> 00:01:23.406
choice.

00:01:23.406 --> 00:01:29.493
Require one hundred percent accuracy with a confidence bound, and no configuration qualifies.

00:01:29.493 --> 00:01:31.835
These controls explore recorded evidence.

00:01:31.835 --> 00:01:36.049
Changing a slider does not create a fresh confirmation.

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:41.069
Now we run a fresh request through the adopted profile.

00:01:41.069 --> 00:01:46.553
This calls NVIDIA Nemotron on Nebius Token Factory using the same implementation as

00:01:46.553 --> 00:01:47.819
the command line.

00:01:47.819 --> 00:01:53.303
The trace shows the actual model output, final issue date, release status, latency,

00:01:53.303 --> 00:01:55.834
and usage cost across every call.

00:01:55.834 --> 00:01:57.522
Live answers can vary.

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:04.130
At one million requests a month, the recorded token mix projects about eighty

00:02:04.130 --> 00:02:09.909
dollars in inference cost for the adopted profile, versus three hundred forty-nine for

00:02:09.909 --> 00:02:10.799
grounded Super.

00:02:10.799 --> 00:02:13.466
Hosting and human review are excluded.

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:19.246
A separate retrospective rules-only comparison completed seventy point five percent correctly without review,

00:02:19.246 --> 00:02:23.247
versus ninety-eight point four for the recorded adopted profile.

00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:29.632
Download the selected profile, requirements, price snapshot, and evidence hashes, then use the

00:02:29.632 --> 00:02:30.521
integration recipe.

00:02:30.521 --> 00:02:34.969
Release an answer only when the final-valid flag is true.

00:02:34.969 --> 00:02:39.417
The evidence is synthetic; independent human validation is still needed.

00:02:39.417 --> 00:02:44.309
The latest noise study preserved answers but failed its latency gate.

00:02:44.309 --> 00:02:47.867
RouteWise makes those limits visible alongside the decision.

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:51.870
The code and complete evidence archive are open source.
